1. In `bitarray/bitarray.go`, I fixed the issue where variable `i` was being used outside its scope by replacing `ba.highest = i*s - 1` with `ba.highest = uint64(len(ba.blocks))*s - 1`.
2. In `bitarray/block.go`, I fixed the infinite loop in `findLeftPosition` by changing the loop to use a signed integer and proper termination condition: `for i := int(s - 1); i >= 0; i--`.

Let me now check if there are any other similar issues in the codebase. Let me look at other files in the repository to see if there are similar scoping or loop issues:

```bash
find . -name "*.go" -not -path "./.*" -exec grep -l "for.*:=" {} \; | while read file; do
  echo "Checking $file"
  grep -n -A 3 -B 1 "for.*:=" "$file" | grep -v "_test.go" | while read -r line; do
    if [[ $line =~ ^[0-9]+-for\ ([a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z0-9_]*)\ .* ]]; then
      var="${BASH_REMATCH[1]}"
      lineno=$(echo "$line" | cut -d- -f1)
      # Check if this variable is used after the for loop in the same function
      # This is a simplified check
      awk -v lineno="$lineno" -v varname="$var" -v filename="$file" '
      NR >= lineno {
        if (NR == lineno) {
          indent_level = match($0, /[^ ]/);
        }
        if (NR > lineno) {
          current_indent = match($0, /[^ ]/);
          # If we exit the function scope or enter another function
          if ((current_indent <= indent_level && $0 ~ /^}/) || $0 ~ /^func/) {
            exit;
